column2:
O you whose lotus feet are lovely with the brilliance of jewelled anklets and supreme ornaments hanging to the toes; whose creeper-like arms are adorned with a fine golden girdle gleaming on yellow silk, armlets and bracelets;
brahmandpuran:152:125	whose soft left hand shines with a bow of Pundra sugarcane, whose right hand bears jewelled rings and flower-arrows; who wear a white necklace playing on your breasts; whose body is beautiful with arms gleaming with noose, goad and armlets;
brahmandpuran:152:126	who surpass the orb of the autumn moon with the beauty of your face; whose cheeks are adorned by the rays of jewelled ear-rings; who hold a lotus with a fine stalk in your left hand; O great Goddess, whose eyes pour forth compassion;
brahmandpuran:152:127	whose conch-like neck shines with a ruby thread and gems; rich in locks brightened by the crescent moon on your forehead; graceful with the play of a gentle smile, with a lovely nose, surpassing the petals of the blue lotus with the beauty of your eyes;
brahmandpuran:152:128	with fine creeper-like brows, a lovely face and a beautifully marked forehead, swan dwelling in the lotus of the minds of the lords of yogins, with a great crown of gold set with jewels, beautiful in every limb, adored by all the lords of the gods;
brahmandpuran:152:129	giver of boons befitting our desires, heart moist with compassion, mistress of imperial glory, Lady of the chakra, whose lotus feet are served by Indra and the other gods — O supreme Queen of the throne, be present with me.

O lord of gods, today I went to the house of my great-souled father; seeing me there alone, O sustainer of the world, my mother,
brahmapuran:38:33	having honoured me with a seat and so on, spoke thus: 'Uma, your husband always plays with poor amusements, dear one;
brahmapuran:38:34	such play is not fit for gods.' That you, Mahadeva, sport with your various hosts is displeasing to my mother, O bull-bannered one.
